;">(4)</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><i style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">For 2025, the amounts reported for </i><i style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">&#8220;</i><i style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">All Other Compensation</i><i style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">&#8221;</i><i style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;"> include amounts provided to the NEOs as outlined in the table below, with respect to (a)</i><i style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">&#160;</i><i style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">the matching contribution that we make on account of employee contributions under our 401(k)</i><i style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">&#160;</i><i style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">Savings Plan; (b)</i><i style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">&#160;</i><i style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">premiums paid by the Company for executive long-term disability insurance, and (c)</i><i style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">&#160;</i><i style="font-family:'Calibri','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">a one-time cash liquidity payment related to previously vested equity, in consideration of the Company</i><i style="font-fa